#import command in terraform helps to import the resource in terraform directory 
#if we have created any resource manually from the AWS Console or CLI.
# Key Notes
#- You must define the resource block in your .tf files before importing.
#- terraform import does not generate configuration — it only updates the state file.
#- After import, run terraform plan to verify the state matches your config.
#- Useful for migrating manually created resources into IaC workflows 


# when we run the import command it will create a .tfstate file where all the instance confiuration are mentioned that we have imported

#if we want to modify any configuration in our instance using terraform then we can copy few values like ami/#instance_type/key_name/tags